# 6. DATABASE SCHEMA

Use PostgreSQL with UUID primary keys, timestamps, appropriate indexes and foreign keys.

All financial records must belong to an authenticated user.

## Table 1: profiles

- id UUID PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES auth.users(id)
- full_name TEXT
- currency TEXT DEFAULT 'INR'
- created_at TIMESTAMPTZ
- updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ

## Table 2: transactions

- id UUID PRIMARY KEY
- user_id UUID REFERENCES auth.users(id)
- description TEXT NOT NULL
- merchant TEXT
- amount NUMERIC(14,2) NOT NULL
- transaction_type TEXT
- category_id UUID
- transaction_date DATE NOT NULL
- source TEXT
- external_reference TEXT
- is_recurring BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE
- classification_confidence NUMERIC(4,3)
- created_at TIMESTAMPTZ
- updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ

Transaction types: CREDIT, DEBIT.

Sources: CSV, MANUAL, AUTHORIZED_INTEGRATION, DEMO.

## Table 3: categories

- id UUID PRIMARY KEY
- user_id UUID NULLABLE
- name TEXT NOT NULL
- type TEXT NOT NULL
- parent_category_id UUID NULLABLE
- is_system BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE

Create sensible default categories:
Food, Shopping, Transport, Housing, Utilities, Healthcare, Education, Entertainment, Salary, Freelance Income, Transfers, Other.

## Table 4: budgets

- id UUID PRIMARY KEY
- user_id UUID REFERENCES auth.users(id)
